<% content_for(:title) { "About — FORA" } %>

<% content_for :head do %>
<style>
:root {
  --blue:     #1b3a6b;
  --blue-md:  #254f92;
  --blue-pl:  #dde5f5;
  --blue-vp:  #edf1fb;
  --gilt:     #b8860b;
  --gilt-lt:  #d4a832;
  --gilt-pl:  #f8f0dc;
  --gilt-rul: rgba(184,134,11,0.22);
  --ink:      #0e1a2e;
  --ink-mid:  #2c3e5a;
  --ink-soft: #5a6e8a;
  --ink-mut:  #8a9ab8;
  --bg:       #f2f4f8;
}
*,*::before,*::after { box-sizing: border-box; }

.about-wrap {
  max-width: 780px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 60px 24px 100px;
}

/* ── MASTHEAD ── */
.about-masthead {
  text-align: center;
  margin-bottom: 72px;
}
.about-wordmark {
  font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
  font-size: 52px;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--blue);
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  line-height: 1;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}
.about-wordmark .o { color: var(--gilt); }
.about-tagline {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 9px;
  letter-spacing: 0.22em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-mut);
  margin-bottom: 28px;
}
.about-rule {
  width: 60px;
  height: 3px;
  background: linear-gradient(to right, var(--gilt), var(--gilt-lt));
  border-radius: 2px;
  margin: 0 auto;
}

/* ── SECTION ── */
.about-section {
  margin-bottom: 60px;
}
.about-eyebrow {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 7.5px;
  letter-spacing: 0.22em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--gilt);
  margin-bottom: 6px;
}
.about-section-title {
  font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
  font-size: 26px;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--blue);
  line-height: 1.2;
  margin-bottom: 28px;
  padding-bottom: 16px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(27,58,107,0.1);
}

/* ── BODY COPY ── */
.about-body p {
  font-family: 'Nunito', sans-serif;
  font-size: 15.5px;
  color: var(--ink-mid);
  line-height: 1.82;
  margin: 0 0 22px;
}
.about-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.about-body strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; }
.about-body em { font-style: italic; color: var(--ink-soft); }

/* ── PULL QUOTE ── */
.about-pullquote {
  border-left: 3px solid var(--gilt);
  background: var(--gilt-pl);
  padding: 20px 24px;
  margin: 32px 0;
  border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
}
.about-pullquote p {
  font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
  font-size: 16px;
  font-style: italic;
  color: var(--blue);
  line-height: 1.7;
  margin: 0 0 8px;
}
.about-pullquote cite {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 8px;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--gilt);
  font-style: normal;
}

/* ── MATH NOTATION ── */
.math-var {
  font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
  font-style: italic;
  font-size: 0.95em;
  color: var(--blue-md);
}

/* ── CLOSING ── */
.about-closing {
  margin-top: 64px;
  padding-top: 32px;
  border-top: 1px solid rgba(27,58,107,0.1);
  text-align: center;
}
.about-closing p {
  font-family: 'Nunito', sans-serif;
  font-size: 13px;
  color: var(--ink-mut);
  line-height: 1.7;
}
.about-closing a {
  color: var(--blue-md);
  text-decoration: none;
  font-weight: 600;
}
.about-closing a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .about-wrap { padding: 36px 18px 72px; }
  .about-wordmark { font-size: 38px; }
  .about-section-title { font-size: 20px; }
  .about-body p { font-size: 14px; }
}
</style>
<% end %>

<div class="about-wrap">

  <!-- ── MASTHEAD ── -->
  <div class="about-masthead">
    <div class="about-wordmark">F<span class="o">O</span>RA</div>
    <div class="about-tagline">Civic Intelligence for Every Person on Earth</div>
    <div class="about-rule"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════
       SECTION 1 — THE PROBLEM
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div class="about-section">
    <div class="about-eyebrow">◆ I.</div>
    <h2 class="about-section-title">The Problem: A World Governing Itself in the Dark</h2>

    <div class="about-body">
      <p>Throughout the world, a disconnect exists between the government and the governed. It is not new — America's founders faced it at the scale of a new continent, where distance (<span class="math-var">d</span>) and time (<span class="math-var">t</span>) made direct representation an impossible equation to solve. They engineered around it — through the Electoral College, through representative bodies, through the postal system. We have since bridged distances with planes, trains, and automobiles. We have bridged time with the telegraph, the telephone, and the internet. And yet the disconnect between the governed and its government persists.</p>

      <p>Today, a citizen is told the way to be heard is to call or write their senator. Being heard is great — everyone likes to feel heard — but the point was someone in society noticed something that they wanted to have addressed, and often that person has some additional information on why they are bringing up what they are bringing up. There are X, Instagram, and Facebook, but those platforms were built for everything except the civic relationship they currently carry. The governed and the government reach for the same instruments, but the connection between them is strained by the platforms built for everything but this — hence the disconnect.</p>

      <p>The information exists. Bills are written. Votes are recorded. Officials are elected. Budgets are published. But it lives scattered across agency websites, legislative databases, news feeds, and social platforms — each built for specialists, insiders, or advertisers, none built for the citizen trying to understand and contribute meaningfully to the place they live.</p>

      <p>FORA exists to change that. Not through protest or advocacy, but by doing the unglamorous work of civic infrastructure: organizing public data, measuring what matters, and presenting it artfully around the issues that shape people's lives. When the civic picture is legible, participation stops being a chore and starts being a right people can exercise with precision.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════
       SECTION 2 — THE MISSION
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div class="about-section">
    <div class="about-eyebrow">◆ II.</div>
    <h2 class="about-section-title">The Mission: Civic Intelligence for Every Person on Earth</h2>

    <div class="about-body">
      <p>FORA is a civic intelligence and engagement platform. Its mission is to reconnect people to the institutions, communities, and conversations that govern their lives — with global reach as a long-term goal — by making civic information accessible, accurate, and actionable for ordinary citizens to form a more perfect Union amongst ourselves and with our government.</p>

      <div class="about-pullquote">
        <p>"Liberty cannot be preserved without a general knowledge among the people."</p>
        <cite>— John Adams</cite>
      </div>

      <p>FORA operates from a single foundational principle, articulated by John Adams: <em>"Liberty cannot be preserved without a general knowledge among the people."</em> Finally, there is a way for people to not only stay informed, but contribute. Finally, there is a way for those in exile to take part in the conversations on their homelands. Finally, there is a way for us to all learn from each other's successes and failures at the civic level. Come to FORA and get to know your community, discuss values, confer on political action.</p>

      <p>This mission is not metaphorical. FORA is built as operational civic infrastructure: a platform that maps governments, tracks legislation, profiles officials, documents civic organizations, structures public discourse, and connects citizens to the full architecture of power that shapes their daily lives. Every design decision, every data model, every feature — from the smallest label to the largest structural choice — is made in service of this mission.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── CLOSING ── -->
  <div class="about-closing">
    <p>FORA is built in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.<br>
    Questions, partnerships, or press: <a href="mailto:hello@fora.gov">hello@fora.gov</a></p>
    <p style="margin-top:14px;">
      <%= link_to "← Enter Your Address", root_path, style: "font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace; font-size:8.5px; letter-spacing:0.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#1b3a6b; text-decoration:none; border:1px solid rgba(27,58,107,0.2); padding:8px 16px; border-radius:4px; display:inline-block;" %>
    </p>
  </div>

</div>
